---
import Base from '../../apps/gps-go/layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../../apps/gps-go/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../apps/gps-go/components/Footer.astro';
import ProseToc from '../../lib/ui/ProseToc.astro';
import { mailto, studio } from '../../apps/registry';
import { site } from '../../apps/gps-go/data/site';

const title = 'Terms of Service — GPS-Go';
const description = 'Terms of Service for GPS-Go (com.yanerapps.gpsgo), a no-root Android location simulator by Yaner Apps.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
  <div class="prose">
    <nav aria-label="GPS-Go navigation" class="product-nav">
      <a href="/gps-go">GPS-Go</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Terms
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/gps-go/privacy">Privacy</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/gps-go/support">Support</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose-header">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede">GPS-Go for Android (<code>com.yanerapps.gpsgo</code>)</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Effective: 4 Nov 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of the GPS-Go Android application ("the app"), made by Yaner Yang, publishing as
      Yaner Apps ("we", "us"). By installing or using the app you agree to them. If you do not agree, do not use
      the app. How the app handles data is described separately in the <a href={site.privacyUrl}>privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
      <p><strong>In short:</strong> GPS-Go changes the location your own phone reports to other apps. It is a
      development and testing tool. What you do with a simulated location, and any consequence of it, is your
      responsibility. Subscriptions are optional, sold and billed by Google Play, renew automatically until you
      cancel, and are managed in your Google Play account. The app is provided as is, and our liability is limited
      as far as the law allows.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. What GPS-Go does</h2>
    <p>
      GPS-Go uses Android's mock location feature in Developer options to make your device report a location you
      choose: a single point, a route, or a position you steer with a joystick that floats over other apps. It
      needs Android 12 or later and no root, it does not change your device's real position, and it only affects
      your own device. You must select GPS-Go as the mock location app in Developer options yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      GPS-Go does not hide or evade mock-location detection. Android marks simulated locations, and apps that
      check may detect or refuse them. Some apps also use Wi-Fi or cellular positioning, which can reveal your
      real location while a simulation is running. Whether another app accepts, detects or rejects a simulated
      location is decided by that app, not by us.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Your responsibility for how you use it</h2>
    <p>
      Location simulation is meant for purposes such as testing and developing location-aware apps, demonstrating
      features, checking how an app behaves in another region, and protecting your privacy. You use the app at
      your own risk, and you alone are responsible for how you use it and for what follows from it. In
      particular:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Third-party apps and services.</strong> Many games, social, dating, delivery, ride-hailing, banking
        and streaming services forbid location spoofing in their terms. Using GPS-Go with them may lead to warnings,
        lost progress or rewards, suspension or a permanent ban of your account. We have no control over those
        services and are not responsible for any action they take against you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Laws and obligations.</strong> You must comply with the laws that apply to you and with any
        agreement you are bound by, such as an employment contract or the rules of a school, exam or contest. Do not
        use GPS-Go to commit fraud, to falsify attendance, work time, travel or delivery records, to evade
        geographic licensing or legal restrictions, to deceive or harass another person, or for any other unlawful
        purpose.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Safety.</strong> While a simulation is running, apps on your device see the simulated location, not
        the real one. Do not rely on your device's location for navigation, emergency calls, safety or tracking
        features, or anything where a wrong location could cause harm, while GPS-Go is active. Stop the simulation
        first. Do not operate the app while driving.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fair use.</strong> Do not tamper with the app, its daily limits or its subscription checks, for
        example by modifying the app, changing the device clock to reset limits, or using a build not installed from
        Google Play to unlock paid features.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Accuracy.</strong> Maps, place search results and street addresses come from third-party services
        and may be incomplete or wrong. Simulated movement is an approximation and is not guaranteed to look like
        real movement to any app.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Licence</h2>
    <p>
      We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use the app on
      Android devices you own or control, for your own purposes, in line with these terms and the Google Play
      Terms of Service. GPS-Go is intended for adults. You may not copy, resell, sublicense or redistribute the app, remove its notices, or
      reverse engineer it except where the law expressly allows it. The app, its name, icon and design remain
      ours. Maps and place data belong to their providers and are subject to their terms, including the
      <a href="https://maps.google.com/help/terms_maps/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Maps Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Free plan, ads and subscriptions</h2>
    <p>
      GPS-Go is free to download. The core features (picking a point, simulating it, the floating joystick, typing
      coordinates, drawing and running a route, GPX import) are free. The free plan shows ads from Google AdMob and
      has limits: daily limits on simulation starts and place searches, a number of route laps per run, and caps
      on saved places, tags, routes and history entries. Watching an optional rewarded ad can add more use; daily
      limits reset once a day at a single global time, shown in the app. Two optional subscriptions are offered:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ad-free</strong> removes ads, raises the daily limits to the most the free plan reaches with ads, and allows unlimited backup and GPX exports. Saved places, tags, routes and history keep the free plan's limits.</li>
      <li><strong>Pro</strong> includes everything in Ad-free and removes the remaining limits, adds backup import, adjustable history retention and saving a session's track as a route. Place searches on Pro are subject to a daily fair-use limit, because each search has a real cost to us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The current features, limits and price of each plan are shown in the app before you buy; prices come from
      Google Play in your local currency. They may change over time. A price change for an existing subscription
      follows Google Play's rules, including any notice and consent Google Play requires.
    </p>
    <h3>Billing and renewal</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Subscriptions are sold and billed by Google Play and charged to the payment method in your Google account. We never see your payment details.</li>
      <li>Both subscriptions are billed monthly and renew automatically at the end of each month, at the then-current price, unless you cancel before the renewal date.</li>
      <li>If a free trial or introductory price is offered in the future, its length and terms are shown before you confirm. Unless you cancel before it ends, the regular price is charged when it ends.</li>
      <li>If your payment is pending, your plan starts once Google Play confirms the payment.</li>
      <li>Upgrading from Ad-free to Pro replaces your Ad-free subscription; Google Play credits the unused part of your current period against the new price.</li>
      <li>The app confirms your plan with Google Play. If it cannot reach Google Play, paid features keep working for up to 7 days since the last confirmation, after which the app falls back to the free plan until it can check again.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Cancelling and refunds</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You can cancel at any time in the Google Play app under <strong>Profile &rarr; Payments &amp;
        subscriptions &rarr; Subscriptions</strong>, or at
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/account/subscriptions" rel="noopener" target="_blank">play.google.com/store/account/subscriptions</a>.
        Uninstalling the app does not cancel a subscription.
      </li>
      <li>After you cancel, your plan stays active until the end of the period you have paid for, then the app returns to the free plan. Your saved places, routes and tags stay usable, but adding more is limited by the free plan's caps. Seven days after the app confirms the subscription has ended, history older than the free plan's 30-day window is moved to an on-device archive, not deleted; you can restore it within the free plan's limits, export it, or delete it.</li>
      <li>
        Refunds are handled by Google Play under its
        <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637" rel="noopener" target="_blank">refund policy</a>.
        If something went wrong with a purchase, write to us as well and we will help where we can. Nothing in
        these terms limits any right of withdrawal or refund that consumer law gives you.
      </li>
      <li>A subscription is tied to the Google account that bought it, not to a device. Use <strong>Restore purchases</strong> in the app after a reinstall or on a new device signed in to the same account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      GPS-Go has no accounts and no servers of ours. Your places, routes, tags and history exist only on your
      device, so we cannot recover them if they are lost, for example when you uninstall the app, clear its data or
      lose the device. Use the app's backup export to keep your own copy. Clearing the app's data also resets the
      free plan's one-time allowances. How data is handled is described in the
      <a href={site.privacyUrl}>privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Availability and changes to the app</h2>
    <p>
      We may update, change or remove features, and the app may stop working in part or in full because of
      changes to Android, Google Play, your device, or third-party map and search services that we do not
      control. We will try to keep paid features working for the period you have paid for. If we stop offering a
      subscription, existing subscribers keep it until the end of their current period and it will not renew.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, the app is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
      kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, non-infringement, or that it
      will work with any particular app, device or Android version, or without interruption or error. We do not
      promise that any third-party app will accept a simulated location, or that using one will not be detected.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or
      punitive damages, or for any loss of data, profits, accounts, in-game items, rewards or reputation, arising
      from your use of or inability to use the app, including any action a third-party service takes against
      you because you used a simulated location. Our total liability for all claims relating to the app is
      limited to the amount you paid us for the app in the 12 months before the claim, or, if you paid nothing,
      to zero.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be excluded or limited by law, such as
      liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for intent or gross negligence,
      and nothing affects the statutory rights you have as a consumer, including those under the consumer
      protection laws of the EEA and the United Kingdom.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, you agree to cover our costs and losses arising from claims by others that
      result from your breach of these terms or your unlawful use of the app.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Ending these terms</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using the app at any time by uninstalling it, after cancelling any subscription in Google
      Play. If you seriously breach these terms, your licence ends. Sections 2, 5 and 7 to 11 continue to apply after
      that.
    </p>

    <h2>11. General</h2>
    <p>
      If a provision of these terms is found invalid, the rest remain in effect. Our not enforcing a provision is
      not a waiver of it. These terms, together with the privacy policy, are the whole agreement between you and
      us about the app. Where the law of your country of residence gives you mandatory consumer protections,
      they apply in addition to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      If these terms change, the updated version is published on this page with a new date. Material changes will
      also be noted in the app's release notes. Continuing to use the app after a change means you accept the
      updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Yaner Apps &mdash; <a href={mailto('GPS-Go terms')}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
  <ProseToc />
</Base>
